  "problem": "For $0\\le t\\le 8,$ the equation ${q}^{′}(t)=0$ has at least\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \nsolution(s).",
  "worked_solution": "The solutions to ${q}^{′}(t)=0$ correspond to the stationary points of the graph of $q(t).$\n\nSketching a possible graph of $q(t),$ we get the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14196843/assets/2fd9e08520f4a671a255f360e583140175650de856a12233962c99a064c4c582.png)\n\nFrom our sketch, we notice three stationary points located near $t=2,$ $t=3,$ and $t=4.$\n\nTherefore, the equation ${q}^{′}(t)=0$ has at least three solutions.",
